# ── GitHub Linguist language detection ─────────────────────────────────────
# MILAN is a JavaScript / Node.js full-stack app. GitHub's language bar counts
# raw bytes, so the large SEO / marketing / legal CONTENT pages (not code) were
# inflating "HTML". These are marked as documentation so the language bar
# reflects what the project is actually built in.

# SEO & marketing landing pages (content, not application code)
frontend/keywords.html              linguist-documentation
frontend/decentralized-social-media.html linguist-documentation
frontend/private-social-network.html linguist-documentation
frontend/best-social-media-apps.html linguist-documentation
frontend/what-is-web5.html          linguist-documentation
frontend/social-media-privacy.html  linguist-documentation
frontend/about.html                 linguist-documentation
frontend/launch.html                linguist-documentation
frontend/city/*.html                linguist-documentation

# Legal / policy pages (content)
frontend/privacy.html               linguist-documentation
frontend/terms.html                 linguist-documentation
frontend/disclaimer.html            linguist-documentation
frontend/cookie-policy.html         linguist-documentation

# Transactional / utility pages (content shells)
frontend/verify-email.html          linguist-documentation
frontend/reset-password.html        linguist-documentation
frontend/offline.html               linguist-documentation
frontend/404.html                   linguist-documentation

# Documentation & data folders
docs/**                             linguist-documentation
frontend/keywords.json              linguist-generated
frontend/*.xml                      linguist-generated
frontend/llms.txt                   linguist-generated
frontend/robots.txt                 linguist-generated
